WEBVTT

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>Having grown up without knowing her birthday or her birthplace,</i>

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.320
<i>the girl, Nadia, who has the stone of destiny, the Blue Water,</i>

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.320
<i>met Jean and the others and set out on a journey of adventure.</i>

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.280
<i>They have finally arrived at her native land.</i>

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.410
<i>Yes, her long journey in search of herself</i>

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.620
<i>is about to come to an end.</i>

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.820
What a huge lake!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.530
There's nothing else around here.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.620
Is this Nadia's homeland?

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.370
Nadia, what's wrong? Hey!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.210
Hey, don't take the wheel without permission!

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.300
Sorry! But Nadia...

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.840
Nadia! Nadia!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.140
Come back, Nadia! Come back!

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.560
Snap out of it!

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.070
Stop, Jean! Go back!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.490
No, I can't let Nadia go alone!

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.370
Grandis, the balloon!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.080
Right! Jean, we've thrown the balloon away!

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.880
Nadia!

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.030
What's happened to that girl?

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.950
It's funny, isn't it?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.120
I thought she was strange from the beginning.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.380
I guess I was right all along!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.590
Is she drawn by the powers of Atlantis?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.720
She looks like she's just a puppet or something.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.260
I believe in her.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.150
Nadia!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.700
Hang in there! What's wrong,

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.200
Nadia!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.120
Jean, I was dreaming.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.870
Dreaming?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.920
A terrible dream...

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.670
The rain... The black rain kept falling.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.050
A flood took place.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.680
My body was empty.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.810
There were so many holes, sucking up water.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.060
The rain wouldn't stop, and washed away everything.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.100
Everybody was drowned.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.690
I kept crying to stop it, but

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.480
my tears just increased the water.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:06.820
Then Jean, Marie, Grandis and the others were all drowned.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.780
Then you all became fish,

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.830
and flowed into my body together with the water.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.380
I heard the sound of a bell...

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.960
Ouch! My head hurts so.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.760
Jean!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.630
What is it?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.840
Jean, I'm afraid.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.890
I'm afraid to know everything.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.930
I'm afraid it will all become real.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.940
Don't worry!

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.150
I promised you that I would come to your homeland with you.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.610
I'll always be with you. Everybody else will too.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.200
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.580
Is it hot in here! Oh, it's so hot!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.830
Damn, what is it now?

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.250
An invisible wall!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.000
What should we do?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.880
Let's go back!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.880
What's that? Are you going to run away now?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.100
No, no! I mean we should take another way.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.810
Let's go forward.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.320
The wall is gone. Let's go.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:30.240
Wow! Hey, hey, Nadia, let me try!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.830
Please! Let me do it! Okay, okay?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:33.660
No!

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:42.380
I'm sorry. But the power of the Blue Water is really dangerous.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.760
Only those who are related to the royal family could handle this.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.140
I'm completely amazed!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.650
Me too!

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.940
She really can do anything.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:08.530
Too amazing. She's different from normal human beings.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.700
This reminds me of the island that sank.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.200
They are the same things.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.660
The same things?

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.660
The heritage of the ancient people of Atlantis.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.460
A dragon!

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.920
Don't worry. It's already dead.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.380
It was an ancient animal.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.840
There are so many!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:35.510
Lots of strange animals are locked in cages here.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.470
What in the world is this place?

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:42.400
This is Noah's Ark from the Old Testament.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.320
Earthmen called it Noah's Ark.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.230
Earthmen?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.860
Ark? This?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.320
Is this giant shaft an ark?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:57.080
Earthmen started to do things on their own

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.500
without listening to God's voice.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.580
So, God decided to remake the Earth.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:08.130
A flood washed across the Earth, wiping out everything.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.510
Only Noah and his family were faithful to God,

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:15.220
and were gathered on the ark so that they might survive.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:20.680
A long time ago, the people of Atlantis began to fight.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:28.440
They hated each other, and killed each other until the very end.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.650
Lots of lives were lost on the ground.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.910
One ark was burned and sank into the sea.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.410
It was called Atlantis.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.420
Another ark lost its master, and disappeared somewhere.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.920
It was that island. It was Red Noah.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:53.300
Then the last ark lost its power to fly and fell here.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:09:00.140
The only people to survive were those here, on the Blue Noah.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.310
They established a kingdom here.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.520
So, this was your homeland?

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.190
That means...

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.360
She's a descendant of ancient Atlantis.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:18.120
I'm the heir of the kingdom of Tartessos.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.450
You mean you're the Princess of Atlantis?

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.620
A princess?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.250
How cool, Nadia!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:31.130
All little girls wish they could be a princess!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:41.810
So, it turns out that you're a princess?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.810
The princess of a magical country!

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:53.030
Nadia! Look, this is just like your Blue Water.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.610
My mother left this to me,

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:58.990
but it can't perform any miracles.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:05.000
However, it does hold a great secret!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.210
What is it?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.120
Imitation.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.290
It's just a hunk of glass!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.670
How boring.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.970
She was cheated.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:30.730
I was brought up as a young lady in a good family too.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:36.070
I understand how you are feeling now.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:40.780
I once visited the mansion where I used to live.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:45.080
All the places I loved had changed so much. I was disappointed.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:51.040
And now your homeland seems worse than that. It looks miserable!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:55.170
I'm sorry! I said too much.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.550
Thank you, Grandis.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.140
But the reason I'm confused isn't just that.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:07.060
As I came near Tartessos,

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:12.690
something foggy in my head since I left Red Noah became clear.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.980
Yes, the other side of me kept telling me

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:21.740
to bring back the blood and the power of the royal family!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.700
Power?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.750
Everything in this Blue Noah obeys my every wish.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.500
It looks like just some ordinary ruins,

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.460
but it has terrible powers awaiting my orders.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:39.260
I'm afraid to go on, because I'm afraid to find out who I really am.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:45.260
If what I've been pursuing is tied to this terrible power...

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:54.190
The one who holds the Blue Water can become God or Satan,

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.230
and destroy the world with its power.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:19.300
Sanson, please go forward. Please.

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.110
It's a dead end.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.620
What's coming next?

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.290
Tartessos is going to surface now.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.710
That's the sound of water.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:12:59.840
Surface?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.640
What's this?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:15.980
Jean!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.850
What is it?

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.190
Are you trembling?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.690
Do you see these ruins?

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:29.370
Thousands of ghosts await the day they can return to their homeland.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:35.830
Jean, please don't let go of my hand! If you do...

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.420
No!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.550
What's happening, Nadia?

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:48.090
No! The grief of all the dead is entering into me.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.850
Why? Why does it have to be me?

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.220
Why did they choose me?

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.360
I don't want to have the power to destroy the world!

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.070
Destroy the world?

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:01.820
Yes!

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:08.360
To possess the Blue Water means to possess its great power.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.450
You can see it by looking around you.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:17.830
What rules here now is destruction, death and me!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:21.420
Nadia! Nadia! Hang in there!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.800
Don't resign yourself to your fate, Nadia!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.380
You must believe in yourself!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:29.090
What's in me that can I believe in myself?

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:32.550
I'm selfish and mean. I always get Jean into trouble.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:37.520
I was always a scared child trying to please the circus master.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:42.730
I didn't say goodbye to the man who I knew was my father.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:48.150
I hate, truly hate myself! There's nothing real in me!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:52.700
All I know is that I'm a terrible girl who has inherited the power of Atlantis!

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.910
Take it easy.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:00.960
The power of Atlantis doesn't have to necessarily be used for evil

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:05.250
because you have the key, Nadia. Don't worry!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.050
That's why I'm worried!

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.050
But there's no reason to.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.300
You keep saying that you don't like yourself,

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:19.270
but you know I love you.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:24.190
You're not so bad. You're just an ordinarily girl.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.190
I'm sure of it!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:41.670
It's amazing that everything's in working order

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.710
even though the kingdom was destroyed and it's gone unused.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:46.340
It's not destroyed yet.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:52.050
I've noticed that the kingdom of Tartessos was not destroyed,

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.930
but changed its form to survive.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:58.020
Really? Let's go find it then!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:58.850
What's the name of the place?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.060
Neo Atlantis.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.770
I'm sure I'm the Princess of Neo Atlantis.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:09.860
I'm Princess Nadia, just as Gargoyle said.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.990
It's sad, but they are my people too.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.870
Where is this?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.920
The center of the palace.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.080
The top of the Tower of Babel.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.800
This...

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.550
This is my homeland, Tartessos.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.180
It's an island.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.680
Electra once asked

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:45.150
what is the real function of the Tower of Babel?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.900
It's a communication apparatus.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.940
Communication? With whom?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.360
Communication with our real homeland.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.860
We use light.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:59.660
Homeland? But Tartessos is your homeland, isn't it?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:06.380
Our real homeland. It's 277.5 light years from here.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.960
Light years?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.260
It's a unit of length.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.130
277.5 light years is the distance

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:19.220
you travel when going the speed of light.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:20.930
Speed of light?

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.230
Light travels 300 thousand kilometers a second.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:29.230
What are you syaing? That distance would have to be on another world.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:39.120
So you mean the Atlanteans are...
That Tartessos is...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:44.830
Yes, we have come from another star.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:50.710
I'm not a human being. I'm an alien.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.220
Jean, take a good look at me!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.590
I'm not an ordinary girl!

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.180
I make you unhappy! I make everybody unhappy!

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.560
I will scatter unhappiness all over the world someday.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.310
Me, my father or Gargoyle will by using the Blue Water!

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:12.360
Nadia.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.360
Nadia...

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.950
Goodbye.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.980
Nadia, it's me. Do you understand?

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:02.160
Jean, what happened to me?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.540
Nadia!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.330
I was so scared! I was so scared!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.380
Marie...

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.460
Nadia!

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.930
Don't be mean to Nadia!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.020
Marie...

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.190
It's not like that. It's okay.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.280
Jean, tell me.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.240
Why was I...

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.330
The Blue Water shone again.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:49.910
The closer you got to the ground, the slower your falling became.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:55.670
You landed on the ground as though someone was holding you.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.210
I knew it.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:03.220
I can't escape my fate and the Blue Water.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.350
Stop your nonsense!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:07.510
You think you're playing a tragic role?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.890
You don't even know how much we were worried about you?

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:13.270
You should have seen how Jean took it! Well?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.230
It's okay, Sanson. That's enough.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.280
How can you keep on living, Jean?

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.870
Why? Because I'm alive now.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.710
You have tomorrow if you keep on living.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.210
Whatever the secret of the Blue Water is,

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.550
or how you are related to Atlantis,

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.590
you're still Nadia.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:44.300
It doesn't matter whether you're an Earthman or not.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.020
I'm sorry, Jean!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.140
I'm really sorry!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.450
I can see some words here.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:16.250
In the name of the fire dragon and the 115th resurrection,

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.420
we here inscribe this life cord

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:22.630
wishing that my beloved daughter Nadia

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:29.100
enjoy hundreds and thousands of days of happiness.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.720
My beloved daughter, Nadia?

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.140
This is...

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:37.730
An inscription written for me on the day of my birth!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.780
So, exactly when does it say that was?

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:49.450
It says I was born in 1875 on May 31st.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.370
May 31st?

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.870
That's today, isn't it?

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:59.130
So today is...

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.460
Probably.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.710
Nadia's birthday!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.550
Your birthday?

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:07.550
Yes, it is!

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:11.260
That's amazing! That's amazing, Nadia! Isn't it?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:14.980
You know what your birthday is now!

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:19.270
My birthday?

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:22.570
Happy birthday, Nadia.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.280
Thank you...

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:32.490
Happy birthday, Nadia!

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.240
Congratulations!

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:47.090
Jean...

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:48.840
Everybody...

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:58.180
Thank you!

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:06.610
Born in 1875...

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.860
That means Nadia has just turned fifteen years old.

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:12.320
I was wondering.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:13.780
About what?

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:20.330
Did your mother know that the ring was a fake?

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:22.670
Oh, well...

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:25.710
I'm sure she knew about it.

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:29.880
Still, she put a great value on it. Right?

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:33.350
Since it was the ring that Papa gave to her that first time,

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:34.850
yes, very much so.

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:40.480
I thought so. I want to believe it's true now.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:48.820
That sound!

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:50.610
